  "notes": "supercombo (ONNX, CUDA EP) with NATIVE_LONG=1 + RESUME_S=3 (openpilot's longitudinal planner + driver-resume nudge), the best arm of the 5-scene openpilot_bench2drive_fixes experiment; all 220 routes, 5 campaign workers; latest scored attempt per route. Early stop from 15 Oct: the routes scored before it were replayed against both rules, and the ones either would have ended were driven again. 23 of 23 source runs kept no run.json, so their routes are attributed to openpilot on the tree they were found in; config.model_env and the rest of config are what 23/23 source runs recorded. early stop (30 s without 3 m of route progress or 4x the expert's time on the route): a car in a driving scene is expected to move, to finish in reasonable time and not to collide, so a route ended this way is a failed drive, scored as it stood when it ended (a collision's penalty included). 6 of 23 source runs ran without it; their routes went to Bench2Drive's own end, so this run does not rank.",
